                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8f79ddbb-84b9-3fe3-95dc-35576984198d",
                        "entry_id": "785692ad-99d4-3998-81f8-d655a8cc0f08",
                        "glosses": [
                            "фотогр. свойство объектива проецировать объекты, находящиеся вне зоны резкости"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bafeb018-ae04-4213-a565-07e7b0b4e046",
                                "sense_id": "8f79ddbb-84b9-3fe3-95dc-35576984198d",
                                "text": "Чтобы добиться эффекта боке на изображении, нужно использовать светосильный объектив — чем выше светосила, тем лучше."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f52e14a4-c892-4e54-8e4e-8a85e870ce3c",
                        "source_entry_id": "785692ad-99d4-3998-81f8-d655a8cc0f08",
                        "source_sense_id": "8f79ddbb-84b9-3fe3-95dc-35576984198d",
                        "target_lang_word": "bokeh",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bokeh",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e8d1c65a-fb7b-365c-a809-563996c13182",
                                        "entry_id": "da391cb3-8839-3b20-9c05-9ca87bb0f90e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A subjective aesthetic quality of out-of-focus areas of an image projected by a camera lens."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83dd7eb0-e3a3-4ac1-9f9b-aa9633030846",
                                                "sense_id": "e8d1c65a-fb7b-365c-a809-563996c13182",
                                                "text": "The quality of the out-of-focus area in a wide-aperture image is called bokeh, originally from the Japanese word boke, pronounced bo-keh, which means fuzzy. In photography, bokeh reflects the shape and number of diaphragm blades in the lens, and that determines, in part, the way that out-of-focus points of light are rendered in the image. Bokeh is also a result of spherical aberration that affects how the light is collected. Although subject to controversy, photographers often judge bokeh as being either good or bad. Good bokeh renders the out-of-focus areas as smooth, uniform, and generally circular shapes with nicely blurred edges. Bad bokeh, on the other hand, renders out-of-focus areas with polygonal shapes, hard edges, and with illumination that creates a brighter area at the outside of the disk shape."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c287e18-bee0-45c1-8602-4d00acff9480",
                                                "sense_id": "e8d1c65a-fb7b-365c-a809-563996c13182",
                                                "text": "Shooting with natural light, I used a long lens (200mm) to compress the space and slightly blur the background by photographing at a large open aperture (f/2.5). This resulted in gorgeous bokeh, putting the city into a blur while keeping the couple razor sharp."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7683c86-dd00-42e6-976f-89e5204f1f6b",
                                                "sense_id": "e8d1c65a-fb7b-365c-a809-563996c13182",
                                                "text": "More expensive lenses usually go down to f/2.8, letting you shoot at faster shutter speeds and get great, creamy bokeh in your background."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "36e02d97-895f-4307-9656-5579fc6190b7",
                        "source_entry_id": "785692ad-99d4-3998-81f8-d655a8cc0f08",
                        "source_sense_id": "8f79ddbb-84b9-3fe3-95dc-35576984198d",
